    <bpmn:process id="W_W3857" name="W3857. Enterprise Fraud Management Strategy, Risk Appetite &amp; Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual strategy (links to VS-33.1); board risk appetite refresh
Frequency: Annual + on change
Volume: Enterprise fraud program (1 program; ~PHP 62.3B revenue protected)
Owner: Fraud Management / CFO
Participants: Fraud Management, Finance/Treasury (links to VS-18), Internal Audit (links to VS-21), Loss Prevention (links to VS-23), Risk (links to VS-21/VS-26), Legal (links to VS-100), IT Security (links to VS-27.3), Privacy/DPO (links to VS-91), Payments (links to VS-80), Ecommerce (links to VS-10), Loyalty (links to VS-13), HR (links to VS-19/VS-103), ABC (links to VS-86)
Source: workflow W3857 — Enterprise Fraud Management Strategy, Risk Appetite &amp; Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3857_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3857_Lane1" name="Fraud Management">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3857_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3857_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3857_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3857_Lane2" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3857_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3857_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3857_Start4" name="Annual strategy (links to VS-33.1); board risk appetite refresh">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3857_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3857_Task5" name="Fraud Management/Finance define the enterprise fraud strategy and risk…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Fraud Management/Finance define the enterprise fraud strategy and risk appetite: target fraud-loss rate (% of revenue, channel-level), acceptable false-positive rate, the cross-channel operating model (central fraud team + channel investigators + store/regional LP), and the governance committee reporting to the Audit &amp; Risk Committee (links to VS-21/VS-36)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Finance / Risk
Accountable (A): CFO / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3857_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3857_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3857_Task6" name="Fraud Management establish the policy framework: fraud policy, investigation…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Fraud Management establish the policy framework: fraud policy, investigation standards, evidence handling, escalation thresholds, law-enforcement referral criteria, employee-fraud handling (links to VS-19.1 discipline/VS-119 speak-up), and interplay with AML (links to VS-86), privacy (links to VS-91), and revenue assurance (links to VS-118)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Legal / Privacy
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3857_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3857_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3857_Task7" name="CFO/Executive ratify the strategy, approve the fraud budget (links to W3864)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CFO/Executive ratify the strategy, approve the fraud budget (links to W3864), and cascade accountability to channel owners (Store Ops links to VS-07, Ecommerce links to VS-10, Payments links to VS-80, Loyalty links to VS-13)
Responsible (R): CFO / Fraud Management
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3857_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3857_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3857_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3857_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3857_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-109 (ensure cross-channel fraud detection &amp; case governance.) | - operational: central fraud strategy and KPI scorecard; operational: explicit false-positive appetite and tuning (links to W3862)
Owner: Fraud Management / CFO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3857_Assoc10" sourceRef="W3857_Annotation9" targetRef="W3857_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3857_Flow11" sourceRef="W3857_Start4" targetRef="W3857_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3857_Flow12" sourceRef="W3857_Task5" targetRef="W3857_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3857_Flow13" sourceRef="W3857_Task6" targetRef="W3857_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3857_Flow14" sourceRef="W3857_Task7" targetRef="W3857_End8" />
    </bpmn:process>
