    <bpmn:process id="W_W3858" name="W3858. Fraud Risk Assessment &amp; Cross-Channel Fraud Typology Catalog" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Strategy (W3857); emerging-scheme intelligence
Frequency: Annual + on new-scheme alert
Volume: 1 enterprise fraud-risk assessment; ~25–40 fraud typologies catalogued
Owner: Fraud Management / Risk
Participants: Fraud Management, Risk (links to VS-21), Internal Audit (links to VS-21), Loss Prevention (links to VS-23), Channels (links to VS-07/VS-10/VS-80/VS-13), Insights (links to VS-28.1/VS-44)
Source: workflow W3858 — Fraud Risk Assessment &amp; Cross-Channel Fraud Typology Catalog</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3858_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3858_Lane1" name="Fraud Management">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3858_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3858_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3858_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3858_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3858_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3858_Start3" name="Strategy (W3857); emerging-scheme intelligence">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3858_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3858_Task4" name="Fraud Management/Risk run the cross-channel fraud risk assessment: identify…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Fraud Management/Risk run the cross-channel fraud risk assessment: identify fraud typologies per channel (POS sweethearting/price-override, barcode-switch, return-without-receipt, refund-to-card, coupon stacking, loyalty-point farming, gift-card cash-out, COD non-receipt claims, friendly-fraud chargebacks, account takeover, trade-account first-party, employee collusion), rate each by likelihood × impact, and map existing controls
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Risk / Channels
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3858_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3858_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3858_Task5" name="Fraud Management publish the fraud typology catalog and control matrix…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Fraud Management publish the fraud typology catalog and control matrix (typology → detection signal → rule/model → case workflow → recovery path), with owners and KRIs, and register gaps into the detection backlog (links to W3859)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Internal Audit
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3858_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3858_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3858_Task6" name="Fraud Management/Insights refresh on emerging schemes (seasonal peaks, new…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Fraud Management/Insights refresh on emerging schemes (seasonal peaks, new tender types, new channel launches links to VS-75/VS-95) and feed threat intel (links to W3861)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Insights
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3858_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3858_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3858_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3858_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3858_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-109 (ensure cross-channel fraud detection &amp; case governance.) | - operational: typology refresh and consortium intel; operational: clear typology ownership
Owner: Fraud Management / Risk</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3858_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3858_Annotation8" targetRef="W3858_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
