      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W3859" name="W3859. Fraud Detection Rules, Models &amp; Orchestration Platform" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Typology gaps (W3858); scheme alert
Frequency: Maintained + continuous tuning
Volume: Enterprise fraud-decisioning platform; ~150–300 active rules + 5–15 ML models
Owner: Fraud Management / IT
Participants: Fraud Management, IT (links to VS-27/VS-113), Enterprise Architecture (links to VS-113), Data Science (links to VS-28/VS-30.2), Payments (links to VS-80), Ecommerce (links to VS-10), POS (links to VS-08), Privacy (links to VS-91)
Source: workflow W3859 — Fraud Detection Rules, Models &amp; Orchestration Platform</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3859_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3859_Lane1" name="Fraud Management">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3859_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3859_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3859_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3859_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3859_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3859_Start3" name="Typology gaps (W3858); scheme alert">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3859_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3859_Task4" name="Fraud Management/IT/EA design and operate the fraud-detection/orchestration…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Fraud Management/IT/EA design and operate the fraud-detection/orchestration platform: real-time scoring at POS (links to VS-08), ecommerce checkout (links to VS-10), and returns (links to VS-32.1), with rules + ML models + device/behavior signals, and a synchronous-decision API within POS sub-3-sec SLA (links to profile §15.3)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / IT / EA
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead / CIO
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3859_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3859_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3859_Task5" name="Fraud Management/Data Science develop and deploy ML models (transaction…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Fraud Management/Data Science develop and deploy ML models (transaction anomaly, return-abuse, account-takeover, chargeback-risk, gift-card velocity) with feature stores, model registry, and champion/challenger (links to VS-30.2/W3862)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Data Science
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3859_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3859_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3859_Task6" name="Fraud Management orchestrate decisions…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Fraud Management orchestrate decisions (approve/decline/step-up/challenge/review/case-open) with consistent customer friction (links to VS-13 CX) and route to case management (links to W3860)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Channels
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3859_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3859_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3859_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3859_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3859_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-109 (ensure cross-channel fraud detection &amp; case governance.) | - operational: synchronous low-latency API and async case fallback; operational: model governance (links to W3862)
Owner: Fraud Management / IT</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3859_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3859_Annotation8" targetRef="W3859_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
