    <bpmn:process id="W_W3860" name="W3860. Fraud Case Management &amp; Investigation Workflow" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Detection alert (W3859); manual referral; chargeback
Frequency: Continuous
Volume: ~8,000–15,000 fraud cases/yr (~22–41/day at 365 days) across channels
Owner: Fraud Management
Participants: Fraud Investigators, Loss Prevention (links to VS-23), Store Ops (links to VS-07), Ecommerce Ops (links to VS-10), Payments (links to VS-80), Loyalty (links to VS-13), Legal (links to VS-100), HR for employee cases (links to VS-19/VS-119), Privacy (links to VS-91)
Source: workflow W3860 — Fraud Case Management &amp; Investigation Workflow</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3860_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3860_Lane1" name="Fraud Investigators">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3860_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3860_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3860_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3860_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3860_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3860_Start3" name="Detection alert (W3859); manual referral; chargeback">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3860_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3860_Task4" name="Fraud Management triage alerts into cases (duplicate-suppress, severity-score…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Fraud Management triage alerts into cases (duplicate-suppress, severity-score, assign owner/investigator), link to customer/transaction/device identity (links to VS-126 identity resolution), and set SLA by severity
Responsible (R): Fraud Investigators
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
