      <bpmn:userTask id="W3862_Task4" name="Fraud Management/Data Science maintain the rules lifecycle (propose → test in…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Fraud Management/Data Science maintain the rules lifecycle (propose → test in shadow → promote → monitor → retire) with version control, A/B champion/challenger, and rollback; weekly review of rule performance (hit-rate, false-positive, lift)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Data Science
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Weekly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3862_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3862_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3862_Task5" name="Fraud Management/Model Risk govern ML models per model-risk policy…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Fraud Management/Model Risk govern ML models per model-risk policy: documentation, bias/fairness checks (no protected-class proxy — links to VS-91), validation, performance monitoring, and explainability for adverse decisions
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Model Risk / Privacy
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3862_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3862_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3862_Task6" name="Fraud Management/Risk maintain fraud policy alignment with payments scheme…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Fraud Management/Risk maintain fraud policy alignment with payments scheme rules (Visa/Mastercard/QRPh/BSP), consumer-protection (links to VS-22/Consumer Act RA 7394), and approve control changes through change governance (links to VS-27.1/W1409)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Risk / Payments
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Per change</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3862_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3862_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
